<% if (it.options.name) { %># <%= it.options.name %>

A repo for shared tooling, made with [mfeflow](https://github.com/mfeflow/mfeflow). It has no apps.
Other repos depend on the packages published from here, and extend the config kept here.

```
packages/contracts   <%= it.scope %>/contracts: event names and types every repo agrees on
packages/tokens      <%= it.scope %>/tokens: colors and spacing
.github/workflows    reusable-ci.yml (the CI other repos can call), ci.yml, release.yml
default.json         the Renovate preset other repos can extend
.changeset           how a change here gets a version
```
<% } else { %># <%= it.scope.slice(1) %>-platform

The shared repo of a polyrepo made with [mfeflow](https://github.com/mfeflow/mfeflow). The shell and
every team repo sit next to it and depend on what is published from here.

```
packages/contracts   <%= it.scope %>/contracts: event names and types every repo agrees on
packages/tokens      <%= it.scope %>/tokens: colors and spacing
.github/workflows    reusable-ci.yml (the CI every team repo calls), ci.yml, release.yml
default.json         the Renovate preset every repo extends
.changeset           how a change here gets a version
```
<% } %>
## Run it

```sh
pnpm install
pnpm build
```

<% if (it.options.name) { %>Build here first. Repos that install these packages with `link:` read `packages/*/dist`.
<% } else { %>Build here first. The shell and the team repos link to `packages/*/dist` until you publish.
<% } %>
## Change a package

```sh
pnpm changeset          # describe the change and pick the bump
pnpm build
```

Commit the changeset with your change. After the pull request merges, the release workflow opens a
version pull request. Merging that publishes the packages.

## Where the packages are published

<% if (it.options.name) { %>Other repos can install `<%= it.scope %>/*` with `link:` paths to this folder while you try it out. To share the
packages across machines and CI, publish them to a registry and use a version range instead:<% } else { %>The team repos install `<%= it.scope %>/*` with `link:../platform/packages/*` paths so a first run needs
no registry. To share the packages across machines and CI, publish them to a registry and replace the
`link:` ranges in each repo with a version:<% } %>

- npm: set `NPM_TOKEN` as a repository secret. Packages are public.
- GitHub Packages: add `<%= it.scope %>:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com` to `.npmrc` in every repo.
- A private registry: put its URL in `.npmrc` and set `publishConfig.registry` in each package.

Creating the GitHub repos and the registry account is up to you. mfeflow never calls GitHub.
